      en: ["At 3187 meters, Kipia Peak is the highest point in South Sudan.", "The mountain's core is composed of ancient Precambrian gneiss and granite.", "Temperatures near the summit can drop close to freezing during the night.", "It features distinct Afro-alpine vegetation, including giant lobelias.", "The peak was first formally surveyed by British explorers in 1929.", "It is part of the Imatong Mountains, an Important Bird Area (IBA)."],
